WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.935
Even now at nighttime, you

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.303
can see the destruction

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:03.937
caused by

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.505
what Ukrainian officials say

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.340
was a Russian missile

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.410
that hit these two nine story apartment

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.277
buildings around

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.580
midday here in separation

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.148
killing, Ukrainian authorities

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.250
say at least one person

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.953
and wounding at least 32 more.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.588
Now, this city is located

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.690
just about a half hour's drive

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.126
from active front lines,

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.828
and it has been pummeled in the past

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.797
by Russian missiles and rockets

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.932
that have hit apartment buildings here

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.068
with deadly results.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:35.969
These buildings

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.171
kind of face towards the southwest

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:38.671
and that is

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.041
in the direction of Russian occupied

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.475
Ukrainian territory.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.978
So you can kind of come to the conclusion

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:45.945
that this

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.213
deadly projectile

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.983
would have flown from that direction.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.586
We can here at night now

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.355
under cover of darkness.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.623
Some residents

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.291
in some of the neighboring apartments

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.059
that have been

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:01.861
badly damaged, working in the dark,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.831
cleaning up rubble and shards of glass

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.434
in what's left of their homes.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:07.867
Missile

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.103
hits here

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.472
and my apartment is this kitchen,

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.608
my parents room and my room.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.943
When it happened,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.946
I heard a loud explosion.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.384
I saw a fire and I covered my head

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.620
partially and on a chair.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.488
And they're taking me up

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:29.355
to their apartment.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.191
There right next to

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:31.524
I mean, they're

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.559
part of the same building

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.894
that was hit today,

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.664
the Russian modules here.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.400
The manager who's here, there's a crater

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.302
right next door

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.870
in the side of the building.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.972
Bible says this does not scare him.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.241
Please give us more weapons.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.843
Imagine how terrifying,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.478
how absolutely shocking

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.779
it would have been

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:53.913
if you were at home

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.783
when this massive explosion took place,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.985
blowing in all the windows

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.420
of the kitchen.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.522
And then to see

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:05.725
just less than a stone's throw away,

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.260
a huge crater

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.762
in the side of your neighbor's building.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.132
And it leaves me with this question

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.633
What possible

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.835
strategic military goal

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.872
could there be to fire deadly

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:22.075
long range missiles at people's homes?

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.577
And Ivan's joining

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.079
us now live from the war zone.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.448
Ivan, on a day of deadly strikes

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.549
by the Russians,

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.550
the Ukrainian president

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.886
Zelensky sent a powerful message.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:36.122
What can you tell us about that?

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.392
He traveled to this southeastern

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.027
Ukrainian city of Mahmoud,

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.929
which has been for months now

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.632
the scene of this deadly grudge match

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.733
between the Ukrainian

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.001
and Russian militaries,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.669
where Ukrainian

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.605
forces have been holding out,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.108
defending repeated Russian assaults.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.911
He met with injured soldiers.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.512
He handed out awards.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.681
He denounced the the air strike.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.048
The missile

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.283
strike ends up Russia

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.184
and on a different

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.919
town in the Kiev Oblast

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.921
that killed at least eight people.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.055
And he stopped at one of these

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.023
convenience stores

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.824
that are all over this country

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.694
and drank coffee with Ukrainian troops

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.563
who took selfies with him.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.964
He's a courageous leader indeed.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.498
All right.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.200
Ivan Watson, thank you very much.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.367
Stay safe over there.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.635
Joining us now to discuss

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.470
what's going on, CNN contributor

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.372
and Russian Affair's Jill Dougherty

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.441
and CNN military analyst, retired Colonel

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.709
Cedric Leighton.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.043
Jill,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.843
how revealing

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.679
are these deadly Russian strikes

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.147
on civilian targets

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.982
so soon after Putin

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.817
and the visiting Chinese president

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.019
Xi Jinping tried to portray themselves

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.589
as working for peace in Ukraine.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:45.892
Yeah, I mean, that's the irony of it.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:46.893
And obviously,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.695
President Putin is saying

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:49.529
full steam

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.664
ahead, this is not going to stop.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:51.965
I mean,

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.733
if you look at the negotiated

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:57.303
discussions that she and Putin had,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.072
they didn't really get into

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.406
any specifics.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.042
They were generalities about peace.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.644
And certainly President

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.746
Xi wants to look like a peacekeeper.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.548
But in actual fact,

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:10.083
I don't think it accomplished

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.217
much of anything.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.418
Most of the discussions

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.187
were really about economics.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.188
And for Russia, that's

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.323
the most important thing. And for China.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.992
So sadly,

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.960
I think this is just Putin saying

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.562
we are going to proceed

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.097
just the way we have.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.966
And, you know, the same brutality

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.302
that we're seeing all over the country,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:29.769
you know, the day

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.738
after the Chinese leader leaves.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:32.872
You see what the Russians

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.573
are still up to.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.374
Colonel Leighton,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.476
what does it do for Ukrainian morale

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.878
to see President Zelensky on the ground

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.713
right near the front lines,

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.615
honoring the fighters of Mahmoud?

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.419
Yeah, it's a huge boost, Wolf,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.388
when the president himself

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.489
comes to see the troops

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.523
at the front line.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.724
And it's really ironic,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.626
you know, when you compare Zelensky

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.094
visiting his troops

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.363
basically in broad daylight

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.965
and mingling with them,

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.033
handing out awards,

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.434
doing the things that he needs

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.802
to do to boost morale.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.404
And you compare that to Putin's visit

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.772
to Mariupol.

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.974
Night and day contrast, literally.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.309
Retired Colonel Cedric Leighton,

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.109
thank you very much.

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.045
Jill Dougherty, thanks to you as well.

